{"version" 2 "boxes" [{"id" "shadertrinket_star_tunnel" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "Star Tunnel" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [380.0 360.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_star_tunnel_code_.kt" "inline" "// Star Tunnel: launch to show it in the window. mainImage is in this box's `fragment`.\nval canvas = shadertoyCanvas()\ncanvas += shadertoyHere {\n    +canvas.rtt\n}\n"} "fragment" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_star_tunnel_fragment_.glsl" "inline" "{{ shadertoy.image }}\n\nfloat hash(vec2 p) {\n    p = fract(p * vec2(234.34, 435.35));\n    p += dot(p, p + 34.23);\n    return fract(p.x * p.y);\n}\n\n// Falling masks invert an increasing smoothstep; reversed edges are undefined in GLSL.\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord) {\n    vec2 uv = (2.0 * fragCoord - iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;\n    float t = iTime * 0.55;\n    float a = atan(uv.y, uv.x);\n    float r = length(uv);\n    vec3 col = vec3(0.002, 0.004, 0.009);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < 48; i++) {\n        float fi = float(i);\n        float lane = floor(fi / 6.0);\n        float spoke = mod(fi, 6.0);\n        float z = fract(t + fi * 0.071);\n        float rr = mix(1.55, 0.05, z);\n        float aa = spoke * 1.047 + lane * 0.38 + t * 1.7 + sin(lane) * 0.5;\n        vec2 pos = vec2(cos(aa), sin(aa)) * rr;\n        float star = pow(max(0.0, 1.0 - length(uv - pos) / (0.015 + z * 0.035)), 8.0);\n        vec3 tint = 0.55 + 0.45 * cos(vec3(0.2, 1.8, 4.1) + fi * 0.7);\n        col += star * tint * (0.25 + z * 2.2);\n    }\n\n    float warp = sin(a * 9.0 - r * 7.0 + t * 8.0);\n    col += vec3(0.03, 0.08, 0.15) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.0, 0.95, abs(warp))) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.2, 1.5, r));\n    col *= 1.0 - smoothstep(1.15, 1.75, r);\n    fragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_star_tunnel_notes_.md" "inline" "Star Tunnel: 48 stars in a loop, each placed by its index and the time, so a for loop draws many\nthings at once. Try changing 48, or the 0.071 that spaces them in depth.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_renderer" "properties" {"children" #{#afield/box "shadertrinket_lead" #afield/box "shadertrinket_classic_plasma" #afield/box "shadertrinket_star_tunnel" #afield/box "shadertrinket_mandelbrot_glow" #afield/box "shadertrinket_sdf_sphere_trace" #afield/box "shadertrinket_camera" #afield/box "shadertrinket_live_stream" #afield/box "shadertrinket_publish"} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "ShaderTrinket window + renderer" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 40.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_renderer_code_.kt" "inline" "import afield.graphics.vulkan.util.Options\n\nprop<Window>(window)\nprop<Renderer>(renderer)\n\nOptions.enableHDR = false\nOptions.enableVR = false\n\nonce.renderer {\n    window = Window(\"ShaderTrinket\", initialDimensions = Rect(80.0, 80.0, 960.0, 540.0))\n    Renderer(window)\n}\n\nprintln(\"ShaderTrinket window ready\")\nstart(renderer::run)\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_renderer_notes_.md" "inline" "The renderer and its 960 by 540 window. Every ShaderTrinket box sits beneath it, and the window\nshows their shared canvas, letterboxed if you resize it. Launch this first.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_mandelbrot_glow" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "Mandelbrot Glow" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [720.0 360.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_mandelbrot_glow_code_.kt" "inline" "// Mandelbrot Glow: launch to show it in the window. mainImage is in this box's `fragment`.\nval canvas = shadertoyCanvas()\ncanvas += shadertoyHere {\n    +canvas.rtt\n}\n"} "fragment" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_mandelbrot_glow_fragment_.glsl" "inline" "{{ shadertoy.image }}\n\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord) {\n    vec2 uv = (2.0 * fragCoord - iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;\n    float zoom = 0.72 + 0.18 * sin(iTime * 0.18);\n    vec2 c = uv * zoom + vec2(-0.68, 0.0);\n    c += vec2(0.08 * sin(iTime * 0.21), 0.05 * cos(iTime * 0.17));\n    vec2 z = vec2(0.0);\n    float iter = 0.0;\n    float trap = 10.0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < 96; i++) {\n        z = vec2(z.x * z.x - z.y * z.y, 2.0 * z.x * z.y) + c;\n        trap = min(trap, abs(z.x * z.y));\n        if (dot(z, z) > 16.0) {\n            iter = float(i);\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    float m = iter / 96.0;\n    vec3 col = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(vec3(0.4, 2.2, 4.2) + m * 8.0 + iTime * 0.25);\n    col *= smoothstep(0.0, 0.04, m);\n    col += exp(-trap * 45.0) * vec3(0.25, 0.9, 1.15);\n    fragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_mandelbrot_glow_notes_.md" "inline" "Mandelbrot Glow: z = z*z + c iterated 96 times, coloured by how fast it escapes, plus an orbit\ntrap (the closest z came to the axes) for the glow. The zoom and centre drift with iTime.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_sdf_sphere_trace" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "SDF Sphere Trace" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [1060.0 360.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_sdf_sphere_trace_code_.kt" "inline" "// SDF Sphere Trace: launch to show it in the window. mainImage is in this box's `fragment`.\nval canvas = shadertoyCanvas()\ncanvas += shadertoyHere {\n    +canvas.rtt\n}\n"} "fragment" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_sdf_sphere_trace_fragment_.glsl" "inline" "{{ shadertoy.image }}\n\nfloat sdSphere(vec3 p, float r) {\n    return length(p) - r;\n}\n\nfloat mapScene(vec3 p) {\n    float ca = cos(iTime * 0.7);\n    float sa = sin(iTime * 0.7);\n    p.xz = mat2(ca, -sa, sa, ca) * p.xz;\n    float s = sdSphere(p, 0.82);\n    float rings = abs(length(p.xz) - 0.98) - 0.025;\n    float band = abs(p.y + 0.08 * sin(atan(p.z, p.x) * 5.0 + iTime * 2.0)) - 0.035;\n    return min(s, max(rings, band));\n}\n\nvec3 calcNormal(vec3 p) {\n    vec2 e = vec2(0.001, 0.0);\n    return normalize(vec3(\n    mapScene(p + e.xyy) - mapScene(p - e.xyy),\n    mapScene(p + e.yxy) - mapScene(p - e.yxy),\n    mapScene(p + e.yyx) - mapScene(p - e.yyx)\n    ));\n}\n\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord) {\n    vec2 uv = (2.0 * fragCoord - iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;\n    vec3 ro = vec3(0.0, 0.0, 3.1);\n    vec3 rd = normalize(vec3(uv, -1.75));\n    vec3 col = vec3(0.005, 0.007, 0.01);\n    float t = 0.0;\n    float glow = 0.0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < 96; i++) {\n        vec3 p = ro + rd * t;\n        float d = mapScene(p);\n        glow += 0.018 / (0.03 + abs(d));\n        if (d < 0.001 || t > 8.0) break;\n        t += d * 0.78;\n    }\n\n    if (t < 8.0) {\n        vec3 p = ro + rd * t;\n        vec3 n = calcNormal(p);\n        vec3 l = normalize(vec3(-0.5, 0.7, 0.9));\n        float diff = max(0.0, dot(n, l));\n        float fres = pow(1.0 + dot(rd, n), 4.0);\n        col = vec3(0.08, 0.16, 0.20) + diff * vec3(0.34, 0.88, 0.76) + fres * vec3(0.9, 0.35, 1.0);\n    }\n\n    col += glow * vec3(0.03, 0.22, 0.45);\n    fragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_sdf_sphere_trace_notes_.md" "inline" "SDF Sphere Trace: ray marching. mapScene returns the distance to the nearest surface, the loop\nsteps along each ray by that distance, and calcNormal reads the surface's slope from it. Change\nmapScene to change the shape.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_classic_plasma" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "Classic Plasma" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 360.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_classic_plasma_code_.kt" "inline" "// Classic Plasma: launch to show it in the window. mainImage is in this box's `fragment`.\nval canvas = shadertoyCanvas()\ncanvas += shadertoyHere {\n    +canvas.rtt\n}\n"} "fragment" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_classic_plasma_fragment_.glsl" "inline" "{{ shadertoy.image }}\n\n// Falling masks invert an increasing smoothstep; reversed edges are undefined in GLSL.\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord) {\n    vec2 uv = fragCoord / iResolution.xy;\n    vec2 p = (2.0 * fragCoord - iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;\n    float t = iTime * 0.75;\n\n    float v = sin(p.x * 7.0 + t);\n    v += sin((p.y + sin(t * 0.7)) * 8.0);\n    v += sin((p.x + p.y) * 5.0 + t * 1.7);\n    v += sin(length(p + vec2(sin(t), cos(t * 0.6))) * 11.0 - t * 2.0);\n\n    vec3 col = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(vec3(0.0, 1.7, 3.4) + v + t);\n    col *= 0.65 + 0.35 * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.0, 1.2, length(p)));\n    col += pow(max(0.0, 1.0 - length(uv - 0.5) * 1.35), 4.0) * vec3(0.35, 0.48, 0.65);\n    fragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_classic_plasma_notes_.md" "inline" "Classic Plasma: four sine waves summed and pushed through a cosine palette. The palette line,\n0.5 + 0.5 * cos(vec3(0.0, 1.7, 3.4) + v + t), is the one to play with.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_publish" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "Publish (share the canvas)" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [1060.0 520.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_publish_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nPublish: the canvas, whichever shader is showing, streamed to the class as @you/field-shader\n(your aaaframe login, or this computer's user name on Field's own relay). A browser ShaderTrinket\nreceives it by that name, and so does the Live Stream box. Needs the Field Electron app.\n*/\nval sink = publishShadertoyCanvas(\"field-shader\")\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_publish_notes_.md" "inline" "Publish, the sending half of the jam: whatever the canvas shows is streamed as @you/field-shader,\nyour aaaframe login or this computer's user name on Field's own relay. Classmates receive it by\nthat name in a browser ShaderTrinket or in their own Live Stream box. Run\nWebRTCNetwork.join(\"https://<your aaaframe>\") once to join a class. Needs the Field Electron app.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_lead" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "Flat Rings (start here)" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 200.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_lead_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nShaderTrinket in Field. This box's `fragment` property is a ShaderToy Image pass: mainImage\ngets fragCoord in pixels (y up) and the ShaderToy uniforms (iResolution, iTime, iMouse, iDate,\niChannel0..3). Edit it and press Alt+Enter to recompile; a mistake is marked on its own line.\n\nEvery shader box below draws into the same canvas, so launching one replaces the picture, the\nway choosing a preset does. Launch this box again to come back to Flat Rings.\n*/\nval canvas = shadertoyCanvas()\ncanvas += shadertoyHere {\n    +canvas.rtt\n}\n"} "fragment" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_lead_fragment_.glsl" "inline" "{{ shadertoy.image }}\n\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord) {\n    vec2 uv = (2.0 * fragCoord - iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;\n    float t = iTime * 0.7;\n    vec3 col = vec3(0.015, 0.018, 0.018);\n\n    float grid = mod(floor((uv.x + 2.0) * 9.0) + floor((uv.y + 2.0) * 9.0), 2.0);\n    if (grid < 0.5) col = vec3(0.025, 0.03, 0.03);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n        float fi = float(i);\n        vec2 c = vec2(cos(t + fi * 1.35), sin(t * 0.8 + fi * 1.1)) * 0.42;\n        float r = 0.17 + 0.035 * step(0.5, mod(fi, 2.0));\n        float ring = 1.0 - step(0.018, abs(length(uv - c) - r));\n        float dotMask = 1.0 - step(0.035, length(uv - c));\n\n        if (ring > 0.5) {\n            if (mod(fi, 3.0) < 1.0) col = vec3(0.16, 0.72, 0.62);\n            else if (mod(fi, 3.0) < 2.0) col = vec3(0.95, 0.74, 0.25);\n            else col = vec3(0.35, 0.50, 0.95);\n        }\n        if (dotMask > 0.5) col = vec3(0.92, 0.96, 0.90);\n    }\n\n    fragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_lead_notes_.md" "inline" "ShaderTrinket, in Field. Launch the renderer above, then this box: the window shows Flat Rings,\nShaderTrinket's default program.\n\nThe program is this box's fragment property, a ShaderToy Image pass: you write\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord), where fragCoord is the pixel (y up, as in\nShaderToy) and fragColor the colour you want seen there. The ShaderToy uniforms are all bound:\niResolution (the canvas size), iTime, iTimeDelta, iFrame, iFrameRate, iDate, iMouse (the window\ncursor in canvas pixels, zw the click while the button is down) and iChannel0..3 with\niChannelResolution. The {{ shadertoy.image }} line at the top brings them in; leave it there.\n\nEdit the fragment and press alt-R to recompile. A mistake is marked on its own line and the last\ngood program keeps running. ShaderToy code pasted from the web works as is.\n\nEvery shader box here draws into one canvas, shadertoyCanvas(), so launching a box replaces the\npicture, the way ShaderTrinket's preset menu does; launch this one again to come back. To read a\ntexture, add textures(\"iChannel0\" to t) inside the shadertoyHere block: the camera (see the\nCamera Input Demo), another canvas (shadertoyCanvas(name = \"...\", inWindow = false).rtt), or any\nField texture. Channels come out the right way up and in ShaderToy's colours.\n\nPorted from aaaframe's madp/shadertrinket.html; dev_docs/madp/shadertrinket.md has the mapping.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_live_stream" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "Live Stream Input Demo (receive)" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [380.0 520.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_live_stream_code_.kt" "inline" "import afield.media.webrtc.webrtcPublishers\nimport afield.media.webrtc.webrtcSource\n\n/*\nLive Stream Input Demo: iChannel2 is a classmate's stream (ShaderTrinket's Receive into iChannel2).\nClick a name in the list under this box. Until you do, it shows the first publisher on the\nnetwork; on Field's own relay that is this document's Publish box.\n*/\nval publishers = webrtcPublishers()\nval stream = webrtcSource(publishers.names.firstOrNull() ?: \"nobody\", 960, 540)\npublishers.onChange { names ->\n    if (stream.target == \"nobody\" && names.isNotEmpty()) stream.watch(names.first())\n}\npublishers.onPick { name -> stream.watch(name) }\ndisplay(\"publishers\", publishers.html { stream.target })\n\nval canvas = shadertoyCanvas()\ncanvas += shadertoyHere {\n    +canvas.rtt\n    textures(\"iChannel2\" to stream)\n}\n"} "fragment" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_live_stream_fragment_.glsl" "inline" "{{ shadertoy.image }}\n\n// Live Stream Input Demo: iChannel2 is the stream picked in this box's list (ShaderTrinket's\n// Receive). The Publish box shares this canvas as @you/field-shader for the class to pick.\n\nfloat hash(vec2 p) {\n    p = fract(p * vec2(234.34, 435.35));\n    p += dot(p, p + 34.23);\n    return fract(p.x * p.y);\n}\n\n// Falling masks invert an increasing smoothstep; reversed edges are undefined in GLSL.\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord) {\n    vec2 uv = fragCoord / iResolution.xy;\n    vec2 p = (2.0 * fragCoord - iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;\n\n    vec3 remote = texture(iChannel2, uv).rgb;\n    float signal = smoothstep(0.01, 0.16, dot(remote, vec3(0.333)));\n\n    float lane = floor(uv.y * 12.0);\n    float bars = step(0.82, hash(vec2(lane, floor(iTime * 5.0))));\n    float sweep = (1.0 - smoothstep(0.0, 0.02, abs(fract(uv.x * 5.0 - iTime * 0.35) - 0.5)));\n    vec3 fallback = mix(vec3(0.015, 0.018, 0.028), vec3(0.08, 0.36, 0.40), bars);\n    fallback += sweep * vec3(0.9, 0.62, 0.18) * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.0, 1.35, length(p)));\n\n    // The procedural field remains visible until a remote stream arrives.\n    vec3 color = mix(fallback, remote, signal);\n    color += signal * vec3(0.18, 0.75, 0.64) * sweep;\n    color *= 0.75 + 0.25 * sin(iTime + uv.x * 9.0);\n    fragColor = vec4(color, 1.0);\n}\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_live_stream_notes_.md" "inline" "Live Stream Input Demo, the receiving half of the classroom jam: a list of everyone publishing on\nthe network appears under this box, and the one you click arrives as iChannel2, from a browser\nShaderTrinket or another Field. Until a stream arrives the shader shows its own procedural field.\nNeeds the Field Electron app.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "shadertrinket_camera" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer"} "name" "Camera Input Demo" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 520.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_camera_code_.kt" "inline" "// Camera Input Demo: launch to show it in the window. mainImage is in this box's `fragment`.\nval canvas = shadertoyCanvas()\ncanvas += shadertoyHere {\n    +canvas.rtt\n    textures(\"iChannel0\" to webcam())\n}\n"} "fragment" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_camera_fragment_.glsl" "inline" "{{ shadertoy.image }}\n\n// Camera Input Demo: iChannel0 is the camera (ShaderTrinket's Camera button is the\n// textures(\"iChannel0\" to webcam()) line in this box's code). With no camera it samples black and\n// you get a quiet prompt-like field.\n\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, in vec2 fragCoord) {\n    vec2 uv = fragCoord / iResolution.xy;\n\n    // Mirror the camera so it behaves like a familiar preview.\n    vec2 cameraUv = vec2(1.0 - uv.x, uv.y);\n    vec3 camera = texture(iChannel0, cameraUv).rgb;\n    float luma = dot(camera, vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114));\n\n    vec2 p = (2.0 * fragCoord - iResolution.xy) / iResolution.y;\n    float rings = 0.5 + 0.5 * sin(length(p) * 28.0 - iTime * 4.0 + luma * 5.0);\n    float scan = smoothstep(0.92, 1.0, sin(uv.y * iResolution.y * 0.75 + iTime * 12.0));\n    vec3 tint = mix(vec3(0.02, 0.16, 0.18), vec3(0.94, 0.72, 0.22), rings);\n\n    // If the camera is off, iChannel0 samples black and you get a quiet prompt-like field.\n    vec3 color = mix(camera, tint, 0.34);\n    color += scan * vec3(0.16, 0.55, 0.52) * (0.25 + luma);\n    color *= 0.78 + 0.55 * luma;\n    fragColor = vec4(color, 1.0);\n}\n"} "notes" #afield/file-inline {"path" "shadertrinket_camera_notes_.md" "inline" "Camera Input Demo: iChannel0 is the camera, bound by textures(\"iChannel0\" to webcam()) in this\nbox's code. webcam() opens the camera once and keeps it open across runs. The first time, macOS asks\nfor camera permission; with no camera, the channel is black and the box prints why.\n"} "nested" #{} "preamble" ""}} {"id" "root" "properties" {"children" #{#afield/box "shadertrinket_star_tunnel" #afield/box "shadertrinket_renderer" #afield/box "shadertrinket_lead" #afield/box "shadertrinket_classic_plasma" #afield/box "shadertrinket_mandelbrot_glow" #afield/box "shadertrinket_sdf_sphere_trace" #afield/box "shadertrinket_camera" #afield/box "shadertrinket_live_stream" #afield/box "shadertrinket_publish"} "parents" #{} "name" "root" "nested" #{}}}] "persistentProperties" ["frame" "name" "code" "code_language" "contents_language" "default_property" "file_proxy_mode" "file_proxy_path" "file_proxy_original_path" "file_proxy_mime" "filename" "preamble" "introduction" "attic" "notes" "geometryReviews" "geometryAppearance" "fragment" "stackSL" "rectSL" "msl" "vertex" "vertex_fragment" "task" "mesh" "raygen" "miss" "closesthit" "anyhit" "intersection" "callable" "fragment_s" "vertex_s" "task_s" "mesh_s" "raygen_s" "miss_s" "closesthit_s" "anyhit_s" "intersection_s" "callable_s" "children" "parents" "compute" "compute_s" "customization" "source_id" "templateId" "_tombstone" "isRemoteJSRoot" "isPythonRoot" ".*_editorState" "metadata" "nested" "nestedIn" "playlist" "pauseList" "bookmarks" "drawing" "panes" "slideShow" "autorun" "layers" "layerFrames" "_controlGroupValues" "keyframeData" "keyframeInterpolants" "ai4_auto_name" "ai4_auto_name_signature" "ai4_chat_history" "ai4_chat_running" "ai4_chat_suspension" "ai4_session" "fileManagerAccessHistory" "kitRole" "isCsoundRoot" "isPdRoot" "isDatalogRoot" "isClojureRoot" "isFieldMLRoot" "isForthRoot" "isLuaRoot" "isMorphoRoot" "isNanoRoot" "nanoLaunchDelayMs" "nanoMemoryInit" "isKotlinJsRoot" "aiStudy" "mainLanguage" "spreadsheet"]}